   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp3ppp/1qn2n2/8/NP1p1Bb1/P3PN2/2P2PPP/1R1QKB1R b K - 1 11",
   "line": [
    "Na4"
   ],
   "spoken": "And it's caught — with both flight squares gone, the queen has nowhere to run and falls. This exact motif once decided a famous fifteen-move miniature between two world-class players, finished by quiet knight retreats to the third rank and a rook-pawn move sealing the queen in. Queens really can be trapped in the middlegame — train yourself to hunt for it.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
