   ],
   "spoken": "A closing thought on psychology — against a gambiteer, do some investigating into what your opponent actually wants. Gambit players crave sharp, chaotic positions; the last thing they want is a dry endgame a pawn down. That's partly why the quiet developing move was chosen. Play the person, not just the board — within reason.",
